+# PII Minimization, Retention & Auditable Decisions (Aegis)
+
+This patch adds services and orchestration to enforce:
+- Presidio scanning & redaction before ingestion.
+- Encryption of raw originals with KMS and guarded retrieval via A2A approvals.
+- Scheduled sanitization of training data and retention metadata enforcement.
+- Mandatory KMS-signed receipts for sensitive retrievals and side effects, stored in MCP.
+- A2A approver hardening (JWKS verification) and linking approvals to FMEA IDs.
+- Lightweight FMEA service to record failure modes and link HIL evidence to FMEA entries.
+
+Key services added:
+- services/pii/presidio_adapter.py — analyze & redact API
+- services/pii/encrypt_store.py — upload & server-side KMS encrypt originals
+- services/pii/retrieval_guard.py — enforces A2A approval for presigned retrievals and requests signed receipt
+- services/compliance/sanitization_job.py (+cronjob) — periodic training-data sanitization and retention annotation
+- services/a2a/approver_strict.py — A2A approver with JWKS verification + KMS-signed approvals + FMEA linking support
+- services/audit/receipt_signer.py — signs side-effect / retrieval events and writes to MCP
+- services/fmea/fmea_service.py — lightweight FMEA store and evidence linking
+
+Operator next steps:
+1. Build and push Docker images for the added services and update k8s/deploy manifests.
+2. Ensure PRESIDIO, S3/KMS, MCP, and Postgres for approver are provisioned and reachable.
+3. Create KMS keys and secrets (originals-kms, receipt signer KMS, approver KMS).
+4. Run sanitization CronJob and verify MCP reports and sanitized outputs.
+5. Enforce that ingestion pipelines call Presidio adapter prior to storing originals with encrypt_store.
+6. Configure approver to require JWTs from your OIDC provider (APPROVER_JWKS_URL) and test retrieval guard flows.
+
